From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] sys_mmapper: place a power-of-two reservation on its own size

Upstream: not yet submitted; written to be upstreamed (generic, no title names)
Licence: MIT, as ps3recomp (see its LICENSE); offered under the same terms
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0017)

What: sys_mmapper_allocate_address (lv2 330) now places a reservation whose
size is a power of two of 256 MB or more (lv2's address-space granule) and
larger than its alignment on its own size (natural alignment), and falls back
to the requested alignment only when no such span is left. Smaller and other
reservations are placed as before (tests/test_loaded_image_memory.cpp's 2 MB
reservation still lands at 0x40300000).

lv2 hands out address space first-fit from the bottom of user space (RPCS3's
vm::find_map searches upward from 0x10000000 in alignment steps), so a
title's few early reservations land on large boundaries. This runtime keeps
its own windows at 0x50000000-0x6FFFFFFF, so with a 256 MB reservation at
0x40000000 a 512 MB one with 256 MB alignment went to 0x70000000, across
0x80000000. Under RPCS3 the same sequence gives 0x30000000 and 0x40000000:
the 512 MB lands on a 512 MB boundary. A naturally aligned reservation never
crosses a boundary of its own size, which keeps that property here.

Why: a title heap that numbers its 8 KB pages with 16 bits of the address
((address >> 13) & 0xFFFF over a 512 MB reservation) saw its page numbers
wrap at 0x80000000. Its page lookup then found none of its blocks, so every
realloc returned NULL. The C library's atexit grows its table with realloc
and, on that failure, returns without releasing its lock, so the lock leaked.
The next thread to register a destructor (a static initialiser) blocked on it
for good.

Test: tests/test_mmapper_hle_heap.c (run by tools/test_mmapper_hle_heap.py)
gains the reservation sequence above: a 512 MB reservation after a 256 MB one
is 512 MB aligned, outside the runtime's windows, and its 16-bit page numbers
do not wrap. A small or non-power-of-two reservation keeps the requested
alignment. The new checks fail without the change, and the existing ones
(and tools/test_loaded_image_memory.py) still pass.

diff --git a/runtime/syscalls/sys_memory.c b/runtime/syscalls/sys_memory.c
index 66eef25c..d8225889 100644
--- a/runtime/syscalls/sys_memory.c
+++ b/runtime/syscalls/sys_memory.c
@@ -344,7 +344,23 @@ int64_t sys_mmapper_allocate_address(ppu_context* ctx)
     int slot = -1;
     for (int i = 0; i < SYS_MEMORY_ALLOC_MAX; ++i)
         if (!s_mapper_reservations[i].start) { slot = i; break; }
-    uint32_t addr = slot < 0 ? 0 : mapper_address(size, alignment);
+    /* A power-of-two reservation of 256 MB or more (lv2's address-space
+     * granule) that is larger than its alignment is placed on its own size first (falling back to the requested alignment if no such
+     * span is left). lv2 hands out address space first-fit from the bottom
+     * of user space, so a title's few early reservations land on large
+     * boundaries; this runtime keeps its own windows at 0x50000000-0x6FFFFFFF
+     * and would otherwise put a 512 MB reservation at 0x70000000, across
+     * 0x80000000. A title allocator that numbers its pages within the
+     * reservation by address bits (seen: (address >> 13) & 0xFFFF over a
+     * 512 MB heap) then sees its page numbers wrap, finds none of its blocks
+     * again and fails every realloc. A naturally aligned
+     * reservation never crosses a boundary of its own size. */
+    uint32_t addr = 0;
+    if (slot >= 0) {
+        if (size >= 0x10000000u && size > alignment && !(size & (size - 1u)))
+            addr = mapper_address(size, size);
+        if (!addr) addr = mapper_address(size, alignment);
+    }
     if (addr) {
         mapper_reservation* r = &s_mapper_reservations[slot];
         r->start = r->next = addr; r->end = s_mapper_bump_ptr;
diff --git a/tests/test_mmapper_hle_heap.c b/tests/test_mmapper_hle_heap.c
index db21e675..dbea4b9f 100644
--- a/tests/test_mmapper_hle_heap.c
+++ b/tests/test_mmapper_hle_heap.c
@@ -86,6 +86,20 @@ int main(void) {
     CHECK(vm_read32(virtual_memory)==0x11223344);
     for (uint32_t i=0;i<VM_AUDIO_SIZE/VM_AUDIO_PORT_SIZE;++i)
         CHECK(vm_read32(VM_AUDIO_BASE+i*VM_AUDIO_PORT_SIZE)==0xABCDEF00u+i);
+    /* A power-of-two reservation larger than its alignment is naturally
+     * aligned, so it never crosses a boundary of its own size: after a 256 MB
+     * reservation at 0x40000000, a 512 MB one with 256 MB alignment would
+     * otherwise land at 0x70000000, across 0x80000000, and a title heap that
+     * numbers 8 KB pages with 16 bits would see them wrap. */
+    reset();CHECK(reserve(0x10000000,0x10000000)==CELL_OK);CHECK(out()==0x40000000u);
+    CHECK(reserve(0x20000000,0x10000000)==CELL_OK);uint32_t heap512=out();
+    CHECK((heap512&0x1FFFFFFFu)==0);CHECK(disjoint(heap512,0x20000000u));
+    CHECK(((heap512>>13)&0xFFFFu)<(((heap512+0x20000000u-1u)>>13)&0xFFFFu));
+    CHECK(reserve(0x10000000,0x10000000)==CELL_OK);CHECK(out()==heap512+0x20000000u);
+    /* Sizes that are not a power of two, or no larger than their alignment,
+     * keep the requested alignment. */
+    reset();CHECK(reserve(0x100000,0x10000)==CELL_OK);CHECK(out()==0x40000000u);
+    CHECK(reserve(0x300000,0x100000)==CELL_OK);CHECK(out()==0x40100000u);
     /* Failure must neither publish an output nor consume the safe gap. */
     reset();vm_write32(0x10000,0xAABBCCDDu);
     CHECK(reserve(0x80000000,0x10000000)!=(int64_t)CELL_OK);CHECK(out()==0xAABBCCDDu);
